WEBVTT

00:09.080 --> 00:10.500
Who are you?

00:10.500 --> 00:12.250
Well, Ms. Mitsugoshi Lady...

00:12.830 --> 00:15.420
Your company is just making too much money.

00:15.920 --> 00:18.380
Tea leaves, cacao, coffee...

00:18.380 --> 00:21.540
A hundred million zeni would be
chump change for this cart alone.

00:21.880 --> 00:26.460
Your business has been growing like crazy,
and my boss thinks it's time for that to stop!

00:30.130 --> 00:31.750
Your boss?

00:31.750 --> 00:33.710
You've heard of Garter?

00:33.710 --> 00:38.580
He controls all the buying and selling in Midgar,
and you ladies went and made him mad.

00:39.960 --> 00:41.170
Oh no...

00:41.170 --> 00:42.540
Mr. Garter?

00:42.540 --> 00:45.040
But everyone knows he's the respectable gentleman

00:45.040 --> 00:47.130
who serves as the president of the
Major Corporate Alliance.

00:47.130 --> 00:51.380
He's a faithful follower of the Divine Teachings
and has made many sizable donations to the Church!

00:51.670 --> 00:57.080
He's certainly not the type to hire a bunch of ruffians
like you to interfere with honest businesspeople!

00:58.000 --> 01:00.460
Then I guess you learned something, didn't you?

01:00.710 --> 01:03.580
Even the most righteous of people
have a hidden dark side.

01:03.580 --> 01:08.130
Garter only made it as big as he did
by making the most of people like us.

01:08.380 --> 01:09.630
I don't believe it...

01:10.920 --> 01:13.960
I don't believe you think it makes a difference
to tell us what we already know.

01:13.960 --> 01:14.960
Huh?

01:14.960 --> 01:18.130
I will admit that there is value in testimony
from an involved party.

01:23.540 --> 01:26.170
Every person alive has a hidden dark side.

01:26.500 --> 01:28.630
Righteous or wicked...

01:28.630 --> 01:30.880
Exceptional or ordinary...

01:30.880 --> 01:33.290
Man or woman...

01:33.830 --> 01:35.830
Women, all in black!

01:36.170 --> 01:37.380
No, you can't be...

01:37.380 --> 01:40.290
Unsheathe the sword of judgment.

01:49.460 --> 01:52.580
It's true, night is best when it's quiet.

01:53.880 --> 01:57.670
I believe we have reduced their legitimate ranks
considerably with this operation.

01:58.170 --> 01:59.380
So now...

01:59.580 --> 02:04.630
Yes, the underworld players connected to the
Cult should start to show themselves.

02:06.290 --> 02:07.500
The war...

02:08.540 --> 02:09.960
is about to begin.

02:17.710 --> 02:19.790
That is too late

02:19.790 --> 02:22.710
You can't catch up with a move like that anymore
Sonna te ja mou oitsukenai<b></b>

02:22.710 --> 02:24.830
That is to say...

02:27.830 --> 02:34.040
The first move chooses an unknown future
Saisho no itte de erabu michi naru future<b></b>

02:34.040 --> 02:36.380
How it will be
Sono arisama<b></b>

02:36.710 --> 02:37.830
This way

02:37.830 --> 02:44.080
The last move decides the world's answer
Saigo no itte de kimeru sekai no answer<b></b>

02:44.080 --> 02:46.710
A single winner
Hitori no winner<b></b>

02:46.710 --> 02:48.080
It's me

02:48.330 --> 02:50.630
These eyes have seen it
Kono me wa misueta<b></b>

02:52.130 --> 02:57.710
The optimal solution no one has yet been able to discern
Dare mo imada mitoosenu saitekikai o<b></b>

02:59.000 --> 03:02.790
It's all a game to control the board
Subete wa banjou shihai suru game<b></b>

03:02.790 --> 03:05.290
A battle of thought
Shikou no tousou<b></b>

03:05.460 --> 03:07.880
I disguise even my mistakes
Mistake sae mo gisou shite<b></b>

03:07.880 --> 03:10.460
And even checkmate is a preparatory move
Checkmate made fuseki toshite<b></b>

03:10.460 --> 03:12.880
A game to take each other's king
King o ubaiau game<b></b>

03:12.880 --> 03:15.330
Ideology and desire
Shisou to yokubou<b></b>

03:15.630 --> 03:18.000
A bad move to not let one chance get away
One chance minogasanu akushu<b></b>

03:18.000 --> 03:20.670
The last chance will cinch it
Last chance kanarazu shitomeru<b></b>

03:20.920 --> 03:22.920
That is too late

03:22.920 --> 03:25.830
You can't catch up with a move like that anymore
Sonna te ja mou oitsukenai<b></b>

03:25.830 --> 03:28.000
That is to say

03:28.000 --> 03:32.960
Total victory is in my hands
Kanzen shouri wa kono te no naka ni<b></b>

03:38.250 --> 03:41.040
No one can catch up now
Dare nimo mou oitsukenai<b></b>

03:42.040 --> 03:47.000
<b>#04 Mask of Falsehood</b>

03:42.580 --> 03:46.250
It's here, it's here, it is here!

03:46.250 --> 03:48.380
All eyes will be right here on me!

03:48.380 --> 03:51.790
Now that we have donned the latest in fashion
from Comme Ça du Mitsugoshi,

03:51.790 --> 03:54.330
the eyes of every girl on the street will be...

03:54.920 --> 03:57.040
...laser focused on us!

03:57.040 --> 03:59.580
First they'll start hitting on us,
and then the smooching will begin!

03:59.580 --> 04:00.880
Guaranteed!

04:00.880 --> 04:02.540
Mmmmmwah...

04:02.670 --> 04:04.790
<i>Comme Ça du Mitsugoshi...</i>

04:04.790 --> 04:07.580
<i>Anything related to design probably came from Eta.</i>

04:08.170 --> 04:10.790
<i>First Gamma, then Beta and Epsilon...</i>

04:10.790 --> 04:14.000
<i>Man, every single one of them is just running wild.</i>

04:15.500 --> 04:16.960
Uh, looks like something's peeling off.

04:16.960 --> 04:17.960
What?

04:18.960 --> 04:20.880
The Comme Ça du Mitsogoshi logo!

04:20.880 --> 04:23.380
Without that, these clothes are just cheap knockoffs!

04:23.380 --> 04:24.830
But on the other hand,

04:24.830 --> 04:28.540
if we stick these on our other clothes,
then they will be Comme Ça du Mitsugoshi...

04:30.580 --> 04:32.130
What a loser brand...

04:33.000 --> 04:35.250
This is the logo of the place we bought these from!

04:35.250 --> 04:37.170
Does this mean mine is, too?

04:37.170 --> 04:40.000
And now that I look at this up close,
it seems kinda off.

04:40.250 --> 04:43.000
The real one is more, you know, intricate or something.

04:43.710 --> 04:45.830
No wonder these duds were so cheap.

04:45.830 --> 04:46.880
Mine, too...

04:46.880 --> 04:50.790
<i>Come to think of it, all of my outfits were
curated by Alpha and the girls.</i>

04:51.080 --> 04:54.290
<i>Everything I'm wearing is like a
knockoff from my past life.</i>

04:56.040 --> 05:01.460
<i>I saw people walking around the capital wearing suits,
and thought that was just the culture here.</i>

05:01.460 --> 05:03.920
<i>But it's looking like that was all Alpha's doing, too.</i>

05:04.880 --> 05:06.960
<i>I guess they're using my knowledge from my past life</i>

05:06.960 --> 05:09.830
<i>to increase their market share
as far as they can make it go.</i>

05:09.830 --> 05:14.210
<i>And I bet the people they're stealing business from
are none too happy about it.</i>

05:14.880 --> 05:18.790
<i>The people they're stealing business from!</i>

05:18.790 --> 05:20.210
<i>Those people aren't happy!</i>

05:21.210 --> 05:23.130
But that all ends today.

05:23.880 --> 05:24.880
Cid?

05:24.880 --> 05:26.210
Taking a dump?

05:26.210 --> 05:27.420
No.

05:28.250 --> 05:29.880
I'm going to reclaim what's mine.

05:30.420 --> 05:31.630
All of it.

05:31.630 --> 05:32.880
What's that about?

05:32.880 --> 05:36.040
Doesn't he know that summer is already over?

05:46.380 --> 05:50.380
<i>As of today, I am a super elite secret agent!</i>

05:52.040 --> 05:55.750
<i>Tonight, the world will know my name!</i>

06:02.170 --> 06:03.380
Welcome...

06:06.000 --> 06:07.420
my dear Shadow.

06:08.830 --> 06:10.380
I have forsaken that name.

06:10.790 --> 06:12.580
Oh yes, of course,

06:12.580 --> 06:14.170
Mr. John Smith.

06:14.500 --> 06:18.670
It is truly heartening to have you
so kindly joining our ranks.

06:18.670 --> 06:22.250
It is a profitable arrangement for myself, that is all.

06:22.250 --> 06:26.330
Oh, but don't you find it depressing to maintain
a relationship based solely on profit?

06:26.330 --> 06:27.580
Don't you?

06:27.580 --> 06:29.250
My, how unfriendly.

06:31.000 --> 06:36.380
The other day, Garter called a meeting of
the Major Corporate Alliance.

06:36.380 --> 06:40.000
Something about strengthening their
measures against Mitsugoshi.

06:40.460 --> 06:45.170
The fall of Mitsugoshi may come sooner
than we had anticipated.

06:45.170 --> 06:46.540
I see.

06:46.540 --> 06:49.290
Our plan remains unchanged.

06:49.580 --> 06:53.960
While Mitsugoshi and the Major Corporate Alliance
work to destroy each other...

06:53.960 --> 06:56.080
We take everything.

06:56.540 --> 06:59.790
We will need you to take action for us, Mr. Smith.

06:59.790 --> 07:01.960
But do be careful.

07:01.960 --> 07:05.880
Behind the Major Corporate Alliance, you will find him.

07:06.420 --> 07:08.830
The underworld swordsman who rose above Garter

07:08.830 --> 07:12.920
and took control of the MCA before anyone
knew what was happening:

07:12.920 --> 07:14.670
Gettan the Sword Devil.

07:15.080 --> 07:17.500
I know the man well.

07:18.210 --> 07:22.000
He's a dangerous cur who will
stop at nothing to get what he wants.

07:23.380 --> 07:25.170
But he's mine.

07:25.170 --> 07:26.880
I swear I'll...

07:37.420 --> 07:39.250
I look forward to seeing it.

07:40.380 --> 07:44.080
In the battle for control over the market
in the Royal Capital...

07:44.080 --> 07:46.830
At the end of the conflict where
money is bought with blood,

07:46.830 --> 07:49.540
who will remain standing in the end?

07:49.880 --> 07:52.880
I will destroy it all, then build it up again.

07:56.080 --> 07:57.670
The moment you've all been waiting for!

07:57.670 --> 08:00.790
The Garter Corporation, friend to every family's budget,

08:00.790 --> 08:03.790
starts our big autumn sale right now!

08:04.460 --> 08:05.460
Listen up!

08:05.460 --> 08:07.830
The battle we're about to face is where
blood is wiped away with more blood-

08:07.830 --> 08:09.040
Outta my way!

08:09.040 --> 08:10.040
Our target is 50% off-

08:10.040 --> 08:11.460
Move it!

08:12.540 --> 08:14.630
Step right up and have a look over here!

08:14.630 --> 08:16.080
Garter's not the only one!

08:16.080 --> 08:17.960
Today we have bargain prices on everything in stock!

08:17.960 --> 08:21.250
Check out the selection at local hidden gem,
Highway Robert's!

08:22.080 --> 08:24.710
<i>Major sales all across the shopping district.</i>

08:24.710 --> 08:26.830
We won't let Mitsugoshi get us down!

08:27.500 --> 08:30.880
<i>So basically, Alpha and the girls have gone too far.</i>

08:31.130 --> 08:33.630
<i>They're selling exclusive products
you can only find at their company stores,</i>

08:33.630 --> 08:34.960
<i>with no concern for local distributors.</i>

08:34.960 --> 08:36.790
<i>And now, they've made enemies
of the big corporations,</i>

08:36.790 --> 08:39.630
<i>and even the downtown shopping district
has it in for them.</i>

08:40.630 --> 08:43.330
<i>Now that they've earned the loathing of
the entire rest of the industry...</i>

08:43.330 --> 08:44.880
<i>Yeah, Yukime was right.</i>

08:44.880 --> 08:47.670
<i>The future of Mitsugoshi is pretty much
devoid of all hope.</i>

08:48.420 --> 08:50.960
I will destroy it all, then build it up again.

08:51.750 --> 08:55.210
<i>They will crush Mitsugoshi, and I will crush them.</i>

08:55.540 --> 08:59.000
<i>I will use the massive amounts of capital that remain
to move to a brand new market,</i>

08:59.000 --> 09:01.080
<i>and start up a new corporation.</i>

09:01.580 --> 09:04.330
<i>I'll invite Alpha and the girls to come on
as upper management,</i>

09:04.330 --> 09:08.330
<i>then I'll just change the name,
and Mitsugoshi will be reborn.</i>

09:08.960 --> 09:12.210
<i>Once it's all over, then they'll understand.</i>

09:13.000 --> 09:15.290
<i>They'll know this was the best choice.</i>

09:17.040 --> 09:19.420
That's out of five thousand zeni?

09:19.420 --> 09:21.670
"You break it you buy it"?

09:21.670 --> 09:24.460
This is why people like Mitsugoshi better.

09:24.880 --> 09:26.250
What did you expect?

09:26.250 --> 09:28.960
That's 1,750 zeni in change.

09:30.330 --> 09:32.250
Is it me, or does that bill look wrong?

09:32.250 --> 09:33.830
Wrong? Wrong how?

09:33.830 --> 09:35.830
I don't remember that being the design.

09:35.830 --> 09:38.000
Oh, this is one of those, you know.

09:38.000 --> 09:41.330
The new bills only just put out by
the Major Corporate Alliance.

09:41.330 --> 09:44.960
That's why everything's on sale today, remember?
To commemorate the release of the new bill.

09:45.500 --> 09:47.670
So what bills were we using before this?

09:48.170 --> 09:49.420
Here.

09:49.420 --> 09:51.170
From the Mitsugoshi Bank.

09:51.420 --> 09:52.630
Mitsugoshi...

09:53.170 --> 09:56.630
Before, we could only use them at
official Mitsugoshi storefronts.

09:56.630 --> 09:59.250
But now we can use them all over the city.

09:59.250 --> 10:03.040
<i>Those punks have their own bank now, too?
</i>I tried to use one with a traveling merchant over summer break...<b></b>

10:04.500 --> 10:06.000
<i>Now that I think of it,</i>

10:06.000 --> 10:08.080
<i>I do remember babbling</i>

10:08.080 --> 10:12.670
<i>some random facts I saw on an MHK documentary 
about banks and credit creation...</i>

10:13.040 --> 10:15.830
But even if there is polarity in the market...

10:15.830 --> 10:19.130
In that case, find a different provider
for a different price.

10:19.130 --> 10:21.580
<i>But my memories of it were so fuzzy,
</i>But liquidity is not a constant.<b></b>

10:21.580 --> 10:23.790
<i>and I ended that conversation fast.
</i>It rises and falls dramatically.<b></b>

10:23.960 --> 10:27.710
<i>But those girls took that MHK information
and ran with it.</i>

10:27.710 --> 10:31.670
<i>Not only did they establish their own bank,
they even managed to issue their own paper currency.</i>

10:32.290 --> 10:34.040
<i>And they've even inspired copies...
</i>What do we do next?<b></b>

10:34.040 --> 10:36.130
<i>I mean, respectful homages.
</i>How about karaoke or something?<b></b>

10:36.130 --> 10:37.330
<i>Copies?</i>

10:38.080 --> 10:40.170
<i>The Mitsugoshi banknote uses multicolor printing
</i>My beautiful voice will shine like a star!<b></b>

10:40.170 --> 10:42.580
<i>and a carefully placed watermark.
</i>My beautiful voice will shine like a star!<b></b>

10:42.580 --> 10:43.920
<i>But this copycat version
</i>My beautiful voice will shine like a star!<b></b>

10:43.920 --> 10:47.170
<i>has cruder printing, and a simpler design...
</i>My beautiful voice will shine like a star!<b></b>

10:47.170 --> 10:48.250
<i>That means...</i>

10:48.250 --> 10:49.250
Let's go.

10:50.000 --> 10:52.670
When I was a child, I had a dream.

10:54.210 --> 10:57.710
I had a one thousand yen bill left from my
New Year's money, and I thought...

10:57.710 --> 11:01.170
Maybe I could make more of them with the
copy machine at the corner store.

11:01.630 --> 11:02.830
The what now?

11:02.830 --> 11:05.290
Who cares?
Give me my money back.

11:05.790 --> 11:10.500
I gave up on the idea after the old man at the
counter yelled his head off at me.

11:10.500 --> 11:11.710
What is this about?

11:11.710 --> 11:13.170
Cid, my money.

11:13.880 --> 11:18.080
But now, I am a super elite secret agent.

11:18.330 --> 11:20.330
And dreams can come true!

11:20.330 --> 11:21.170
Cid!

11:21.170 --> 11:22.000
Cid!

11:22.000 --> 11:24.250
Come on, brain! Remember!

11:24.250 --> 11:26.420
I'm counting on you, MHK!

11:26.420 --> 11:27.670
Cid!

11:27.670 --> 11:29.830
Cid, my money!

11:35.460 --> 11:38.790
This single gold coin multiplies into
several times what it was.

11:39.250 --> 11:43.790
But what we find there is the
fleeting illusion we call "credit."

11:46.750 --> 11:50.130
Are you, perchance, talking about paper money?

11:50.130 --> 11:53.380
These scraps of paper, considered by the masses
to be no different than currency,

11:53.380 --> 11:55.080
are, more precisely, not currency at all.

11:55.080 --> 11:58.960
In reality, they are no more than claim checks
for coins that have been left in the care of the bank.

11:59.330 --> 12:02.250
Let's say, for example, you have put
ten thousand zeni in the bank.

12:02.250 --> 12:04.750
In exchange, you are given a banknote
for ten thousand zeni,

12:04.750 --> 12:07.290
which you can use to purchase goods and services.

12:07.830 --> 12:11.170
But this is where something strange occurs.

12:12.000 --> 12:15.630
You have ten thousand zeni in the bank,
and ten thousand zeni in a banknote.

12:15.630 --> 12:18.540
At some point, your zeni
has doubled to twenty thousand.

12:19.580 --> 12:23.580
If the ten thousand zeni in the bank remains
dormant in its vault, there is no problem.

12:24.330 --> 12:27.330
Because even if the money had, in fact, doubled,

12:27.330 --> 12:30.250
as long as only the original ten thousand zeni
circulates through the market,

12:30.250 --> 12:31.960
there is no contradiction.

12:32.710 --> 12:35.750
But the bank has used the
ten thousand zeni deposited there

12:35.750 --> 12:38.000
as collateral to lend out even more money.

12:38.000 --> 12:42.790
The prosperous economy of the capital stemmed from
the business developments of Mitsugoshi itself.

12:42.790 --> 12:46.540
Seeing a good opportunity, the merchants
wished to borrow some capital,

12:46.540 --> 12:50.290
and the bank met the demand by
supplying paper money.

12:50.790 --> 12:53.830
No one wants to walk around with
heavy coins in their wallets.

12:53.830 --> 12:58.380
Use of paper money spread like wildfire,
further obscuring the currency's true value.

12:58.670 --> 13:01.540
The ten thousand zeni in the vault,
multiplied to several times what it was,

13:01.540 --> 13:03.080
circulated throughout the capital.

13:03.080 --> 13:07.080
And Mitsugoshi gained exponential profits by
reaping the rewards of the interest.

13:07.830 --> 13:10.460
This is the true value of credit creation.

13:10.460 --> 13:12.580
"Credit creation"...

13:12.580 --> 13:14.500
What a fitting expression.

13:14.750 --> 13:17.210
Through these means,

13:17.210 --> 13:20.790
a scrap of paper not even worth a copper coin
is given more value than gold.

13:20.790 --> 13:24.250
The leader of Mitsugoshi Bank must be
an extraordinary con artist.

13:24.750 --> 13:26.670
What might this person be like, I wonder?

13:26.670 --> 13:29.580
If I ever have the chance,
I would love to have a chat with this individual.

13:30.710 --> 13:35.500
But is a piece of paper truly worth
the credit people give it?

13:38.830 --> 13:40.790
Compare the two.
Do you notice anything?

13:41.830 --> 13:44.630
You mean the presence of a watermark
in one but not the other?

13:44.630 --> 13:48.630
And, I might add, the Major Corporate Alliance
bill has a rougher design.

13:48.630 --> 13:51.170
Rougher printing, rougher edges...

13:51.170 --> 13:53.290
Do you know what this means?

13:55.290 --> 13:57.380
It would be easy to fake?

13:59.210 --> 14:00.960
We create fake money.

14:00.960 --> 14:03.460
And we'll make a fortune in counterfeit bills!

14:07.540 --> 14:09.250
Excuse me, Mr. Smith.

14:10.080 --> 14:12.130
As you are no doubt aware,

14:12.130 --> 14:16.250
the Major Corporate Alliance bills are still
only in circulation in the Royal Capital.

14:16.920 --> 14:20.130
If we forged them, the authorities would
immediately trace them to the source.

14:20.630 --> 14:21.630
Huh?!

14:21.880 --> 14:25.170
If done on a small scale, I'm sure it could be
accomplished without discovery.

14:25.170 --> 14:28.000
But the amount we would earn would be
hardly more than a child's allowance.

14:28.250 --> 14:30.250
How do you propose we-

14:34.710 --> 14:35.920
Mr-

14:35.920 --> 14:37.290
Is that really...

14:37.920 --> 14:39.960
Is that really what you think?

14:42.170 --> 14:44.670
This is the true value of credit creation.

14:46.290 --> 14:47.500
You can't mean...

14:48.290 --> 14:52.580
If we did make and circulate a large quantity of
counterfeit bills in a short period of time,

14:52.580 --> 14:54.290
naturally we would be discovered.

14:54.290 --> 14:58.670
And rumors of the bills would reach the ears of
the general public almost immediately.

14:58.960 --> 15:03.380
At that point, the citizens would harbor doubts
about the contents of their own wallets.

15:03.750 --> 15:06.750
The credit given to that paper would be lost!

15:06.750 --> 15:07.750
Huh?!

15:07.750 --> 15:10.330
The discovery of the counterfeiting was
already integrated into the plan-

15:10.330 --> 15:12.630
No, the discovery was the plan!

15:12.630 --> 15:14.880
When the people start to doubt
the value of the paper,

15:14.880 --> 15:17.790
they'll make a run on the bank
to exchange it for gold!

15:17.790 --> 15:21.790
If we're one step ahead of the game,
we can monopolize the profits!

15:21.790 --> 15:23.710
That's what you've been planning all along!

15:29.580 --> 15:30.790
Is that really...

15:31.710 --> 15:33.540
...what you think?

15:42.210 --> 15:43.420
Yes.

15:43.420 --> 15:44.830
It is what I think.

15:46.500 --> 15:50.460
This plan is utterly flawless.

16:00.790 --> 16:02.630
That is exactly right.

16:11.130 --> 16:13.670
In the end, he was testing my sincerity.

16:14.380 --> 16:18.960
If I had given in to the pressure and rattled off
some thoughtless babblings, then I...

16:21.210 --> 16:25.580
John Smith, the man formerly known as Shadow...

16:39.920 --> 16:44.000
<i>The mysterious man secretly scheming while Mitsugoshi
and the Major Corporate Alliance battle it out,</i>

16:44.000 --> 16:45.210
<i>John Smith.</i>

16:45.460 --> 16:48.750
<i>He hides his identity,
and carries out his mission alone.</i>

16:49.000 --> 16:53.880
<i>I am the man who betrays his organization
in order to save it, the Super Elite Secret Agent.</i>

16:54.460 --> 16:56.420
<i>What could be cooler than that?</i>

16:57.000 --> 16:58.420
Gimme more, Boss!

17:01.460 --> 17:03.210
<i>What does she think she's doing?</i>

17:03.580 --> 17:05.080
Gimme more, Boss!

17:05.080 --> 17:06.290
Gimme more!

17:15.380 --> 17:16.750
You smell like foxes.

17:16.750 --> 17:18.580
Yeah, I was hanging out with-

17:18.580 --> 17:20.130
I was hunting foxes.

17:20.130 --> 17:21.420
Hunting?!

17:21.420 --> 17:22.630
Delta wants to hunt!

17:22.630 --> 17:25.080
Sorry, the fox is already hunted.

17:25.380 --> 17:27.290
And would you get off of me already?

17:27.290 --> 17:28.040
No!

17:28.040 --> 17:30.000
What are you doing in the capital any-

17:31.420 --> 17:35.000
Delta woke up early this morning,
ate lots and lots of meat,

17:35.000 --> 17:36.830
and came to the capital for the first time in forever!

17:36.830 --> 17:38.540
So why did you come to the capital?

17:38.540 --> 17:40.500
Delta was hunting!

17:40.500 --> 17:42.130
And why were you hunting?

17:42.130 --> 17:45.500
Delta did so much hunting!
Wanna hunt with me, Boss?

17:45.500 --> 17:47.080
Why were you hunting?

17:47.080 --> 17:50.170
Lady Alpha told me to!
Wanna hunt with me, Boss?

17:50.750 --> 17:52.250
So Alpha told you to do it.

17:52.250 --> 17:54.420
Uh-huh!
Wanna hunt with me, Boss?

17:54.420 --> 17:56.250
What have you been hunting?

17:56.250 --> 17:58.960
Bandits!
You like hunting bandits, too, Boss!

17:58.960 --> 18:02.250
Yeah, I do like hunting bandits, too.

18:02.250 --> 18:03.460
Hunt with me!

18:03.460 --> 18:05.210
I don't think I can right now.

18:05.330 --> 18:06.670
No, hunt with me!

18:06.670 --> 18:07.920
Hold your horses.

18:07.920 --> 18:10.960
Didn't you come to the capital for a specific reason?

18:11.380 --> 18:12.580
Specific reason?

18:12.580 --> 18:14.540
Didn't Alpha want to see you?

18:15.960 --> 18:17.170
Lady Alpha!

18:17.170 --> 18:18.210
Did you forget?

18:18.210 --> 18:19.420
Yeah, I forgot.

18:19.960 --> 18:21.460
She's gonna be so mad at me!

18:21.920 --> 18:23.330
You'd better hurry and see her.

18:24.460 --> 18:26.420
But our bandit hunt...

18:28.710 --> 18:33.920
<i>Looking at Delta reminds me of John,
the pet I had in my past life.</i>

18:34.750 --> 18:37.420
<b>Body found dead of unknown cause.</b>

18:34.750 --> 18:37.420
<b>Fourth incident this month.</b>

18:35.540 --> 18:37.420
Another failure?

18:37.500 --> 18:41.630
Yes, um, their private soldiers are
more powerful than we anticipated.

18:41.630 --> 18:44.830
So the would-be bandits are useless.

18:44.830 --> 18:47.080
In that case, I'll send the Clovers after them.

18:47.080 --> 18:48.500
The Clovers?

18:48.830 --> 18:52.000
The elite assassins you hand-picked
yourself, Mr. Gettan?

18:52.000 --> 18:55.830
With them on the job,
Mitsugoshi's secrets are as good as ours!

19:08.130 --> 19:10.710
<i>Delta is fundamentally incapable of
following the command, "stay."</i>

19:10.710 --> 19:13.630
<i>Her brand of hunting is a one-sided massacre.</i>

19:13.630 --> 19:15.960
<i>It makes gathering treasure easier, but...</i>

19:16.670 --> 19:19.250
<i>I miss out on the element of enjoying the battle.</i>

19:19.630 --> 19:21.250
Stop! Wait a minute!

19:22.250 --> 19:24.290
You're Sara, aren't you?
It's me!

19:24.290 --> 19:25.960
You know? Me! Me!

19:25.960 --> 19:27.710
It's me, Zabra!

19:27.710 --> 19:29.330
You remember, don't you, Sara?

19:32.000 --> 19:33.580
You smell like my dad.

19:33.580 --> 19:34.920
That's right.

19:34.920 --> 19:36.790
I'm your big brother, Zabra.

19:37.290 --> 19:39.710
But how are you even alive?

19:39.710 --> 19:42.330
I heard you got possessed and Dad hunted you.

19:42.880 --> 19:45.420
Delta is the best at hide-and-seek.

19:45.630 --> 19:48.750
Delta? Is that what you call yourself now?

19:49.330 --> 19:51.460
Anyway, Sara, you can just let me go, right?

19:51.460 --> 19:53.830
I'm working for the great Gettan now.

19:53.830 --> 19:55.670
You know him right?
The legendary-

19:57.000 --> 19:58.920
I don't want a weak brother.

19:59.290 --> 20:01.920
Did you really want to do that?
He was your brother.

20:02.710 --> 20:05.290
Weaklings bring shame to the family.

20:05.290 --> 20:06.540
Oh, okay.

20:06.540 --> 20:09.040
Delta's dad is the chief of our clan!

20:09.040 --> 20:12.330
He has lots of lovers, and over a thousand children!

20:13.500 --> 20:15.170
Then I guess one less won't hurt him.

20:15.170 --> 20:16.750
The weak die.

20:16.750 --> 20:18.170
If there aren't enough, we make more.

20:18.170 --> 20:19.670
That's the law of the clan!

20:19.920 --> 20:22.580
<i>That's a therianthrope for you.
They do things on a different scale.</i>

20:22.580 --> 20:25.500
<i>You do find the occasional intelligent therianthrope,</i>

20:25.500 --> 20:29.460
<i>but there's a reason most people assume they're
a bunch of "might makes right" types.</i>

20:29.830 --> 20:33.000
Maybe I should go visit
the therianthrope lands sometime.

20:34.000 --> 20:35.670
I just had a great idea!

20:35.670 --> 20:37.330
You can be our chief, Boss!

20:37.330 --> 20:38.540
What?

20:38.540 --> 20:40.540
If you beat my dad, you'll be the chief!

20:40.540 --> 20:43.580
Then you can have lots of babies,
and we'll be the strongest clan ever!

20:43.580 --> 20:44.790
Not happening.

20:44.790 --> 20:47.380
Yes, happening!
I'll get a hundred women for you!

20:47.380 --> 20:49.080
And Delta will have a hundred babies!

20:49.080 --> 20:50.540
No way, not a chance.

20:50.540 --> 20:52.630
This hunt is over.
We're going home.

20:55.880 --> 20:57.710
Zabra has been defeated, you say?

20:57.710 --> 20:58.750
Yes, sir.

20:58.750 --> 21:03.080
One of our underground hideouts was attacked,
and we found his body inside.

21:03.330 --> 21:07.040
And, um, Mr. Gettan, in these last few months,

21:07.040 --> 21:10.040
our numbers have been reduced to practically nothing.

21:10.040 --> 21:13.750
If this keeps up, it will affect the personnel
we have running our public enterprises.

21:14.380 --> 21:18.000
We invested a fair amount of capital
in establishing our bank.

21:18.000 --> 21:21.000
And the amount of money that went to bribing
the legislators to let us print our money

21:21.000 --> 21:22.960
is nothing to be sneezed at.

21:22.960 --> 21:26.250
What do you say to stepping back and reevaluating...

21:26.250 --> 21:27.420
Garter...

21:28.290 --> 21:31.170
You are in a position to control all
commerce in the city.

21:31.920 --> 21:35.880
Surely you have not forgotten who it was
that put you in that position?

21:35.880 --> 21:38.630
N-no, sir!
No, of course I haven't!

21:38.630 --> 21:41.420
All you need to do is follow orders...

21:42.040 --> 21:43.460
My orders.

21:45.670 --> 21:48.920
At any rate, Zabra was the weakest of the Clovers.

21:49.500 --> 21:51.580
Summon the three that are left.

21:52.080 --> 21:55.920
Strengthen our offense against Mitsugoshi,
and take all of their trade secrets.

21:55.920 --> 21:57.290
Y-yes, sir!

22:00.630 --> 22:03.670
Mitsugoshi is tougher than I thought.

22:04.250 --> 22:07.170
Now I see why the Cult labeled them as a threat.

22:24.380 --> 22:28.250
An endlessly deep dark night
Doko made mo fukai yamiyo to<b></b>

22:28.250 --> 22:31.080
I thought, as I closed my eyes
Omotte me o tsubutteta<b></b>

22:31.080 --> 22:36.290
Still unaware of the voice of the star calling out to me
Yobikakeru hoshi no koe ni kizukenai mama<b></b>

22:36.670 --> 22:40.630
A faint light, not too bright
Mabushiku wa nai awai hi<b></b>

22:40.630 --> 22:43.380
But comforting, that's how you were
Kokochi ii sonna anata o<b></b>

22:43.380 --> 22:47.250
Before I knew it, I was following you with my eyes
Shiranu uchi ni me de oikaketa<b></b>

22:47.250 --> 22:49.830
Even if I run out of breath
Iki o kirashite<b></b>

22:50.250 --> 22:53.290
And start to stumble
Motsuresou ni natte mo<b></b>

22:53.290 --> 22:55.540
I've never felt this before
Kono kimochi wa hajimete<b></b>

22:55.540 --> 22:59.460
I can't stop the feeling
Mita koto no nai jibun ni aeru<b></b>

22:59.830 --> 23:03.290
That I can meet a me I've never seen before
Yokan ga tomaranai<b></b>

23:03.790 --> 23:06.710
I run down the path in front of me
Me no mae no michi o hashiru<b></b>

23:06.710 --> 23:09.790
I run far, even when I'm lost
Tooku, mayotte mo<b></b>

23:09.790 --> 23:13.630
If I look up, you won't have changed
Miagereba anata wa kawaranaide<b></b>

23:13.630 --> 23:16.000
You'll be there
Soko ni iru koto o<b></b>

23:16.000 --> 23:18.960
It may be strange, but I can believe it
Fushigi demo shinjirareru<b></b>

23:18.960 --> 23:22.000
Kaze ga tsuyoi hi mo
Even on windy days<b></b>

23:22.000 --> 23:26.500
I don't have to try to reach over you
Over you todokeyou to shinakutatte ii<b></b>

23:26.500 --> 23:28.830
Hey (Did you know?)
Nee (Shitteru?)<b></b>

23:28.830 --> 23:31.880
As all the stars revolve
Subete no hoshi ga mawarinagara<b></b>

23:31.880 --> 23:35.130
I keep my sights on you
Anata o mezashiteru<b></b>

23:35.130 --> 23:38.080
Polaris in the Night
